</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Maximum Path Length <math id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (for PATHCONV)</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We observed average reasoning chains of roughly 5–6 steps. Table <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Maximum Path Length 𝐿 (for PATHCONV) ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameters ‣ All Roads Lead to Rome: Graph-Based Confidence Estimation for Large Language Model Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows that <math id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L{=}12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L{=}12</annotation></semantics></math> avoids truncation errors seen at <math id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>; larger caps (<math id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L{\geq}15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L{\geq}15</annotation></semantics></math>) yield no meaningful AUROC gains and only modest ECE improvements, so <math id="A4.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L{=}12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L{=}12</annotation></semantics></math> remains our default for efficiency.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Impact of maximum path length <math id="A4.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (PATHCONV).</figcaption>
